                'excerpt'        => 'Looking for the best TWS earbuds under ₹2000? We compared sound quality, battery life, ANC, and comfort across boAt, Noise, Boult, and more to find the top 10 wireless earbuds in India.',
                'content'        => '<h2>Why TWS Earbuds Have Taken Over India</h2><p>True Wireless Stereo (TWS) earbuds have become the most popular audio accessory in India. No tangled wires, compact charging cases, and surprisingly good sound — all under ₹2000. But with hundreds of options from boAt, Noise, Boult, PTron, and Mivi flooding the market, choosing the right pair can be overwhelming.</p><h2>What to Look for in Budget TWS Earbuds</h2><p>Before we dive into our picks, here is what matters most:</p><ul><li><strong>Driver size:</strong> Bigger drivers (10mm-13mm) generally produce richer bass. Look for at least 10mm drivers for punchy sound.</li><li><strong>Battery life:</strong> A minimum of 5 hours per charge with 20+ hours from the case is the sweet spot.</li><li><strong>Bluetooth version:</strong> BT 5.2 or higher ensures stable connectivity and lower latency for gaming.</li><li><strong>Water resistance:</strong> IPX4 or higher is essential if you plan to use them during workouts.</li><li><strong>ANC:</strong> Active Noise Cancellation at this price range is basic but still useful for commutes.</li></ul><h2>Top 10 TWS Earbuds Under ₹2000</h2><h3>1. boAt Airdopes Series</h3><p>boAt dominates the budget TWS market in India for good reason. Their Airdopes lineup offers powerful bass, 30+ hour total battery, IPX5 rating, and beast mode for low latency gaming. The ASAP charge feature gives 60 minutes of playback from just 5 minutes of charging.</p><h3>2. Noise Buds Series</h3><p>Noise earbuds come with hybrid ANC, transparency mode, and Instacharge. Their quad-mic setup handles call clarity well even in noisy environments. Great for office commuters.</p><h3>3. Boult Audio Z-Series</h3><p>Boult offers some of the best bass in this range thanks to their Zen ENC mics and extra-large 13mm drivers. The low-latency gaming mode is a standout feature for BGMI and Free Fire players.</p><h3>4. PTron Bassbuds</h3><p>PTron delivers incredible value — decent sound, touch controls, and USB-C charging under ₹1000. Perfect as a backup pair or a first-time TWS purchase.</p><h3>5. Mivi DuoPods</h3><p>Made-in-India brand Mivi offers studio-quality sound with powerful bass drivers. Their earbuds are lightweight, comfortable for long listening sessions, and come with a 1-year warranty.</p><h2>Quick Comparison Table</h2><p><strong>Best for Bass:</strong> Boult Z-Series (13mm drivers)<br><strong>Best for Calls:</strong> Noise Buds (quad-mic ENC)<br><strong>Best Battery:</strong> boAt Airdopes (30+ hours total)<br><strong>Best Value:</strong> PTron Bassbuds (under ₹1000)<br><strong>Best for Gaming:</strong> boAt with Beast Mode (60ms latency)</p><h2>How to Pick the Right One for You</h2><p>If you prioritise bass and music, go with Boult or boAt. If call quality matters more (work calls, meetings), Noise is the winner. For gaming, look for any pair with a dedicated low-latency mode. And if budget is tight, PTron gives you 80% of the experience at half the price.</p><blockquote>The best TWS earbuds are the ones that match your daily use — not the ones with the longest spec sheet. Browse our full TWS earbuds collection at Jikra to find your perfect pair.</blockquote>',
