                'content'        => '<h2>The Great Wireless Audio Debate</h2><p>You have decided to go wireless — smart move. But now comes the real question: neckband or TWS earbuds? Both have passionate fans, and both have genuine strengths. Let us settle this once and for all.</p><h2>Neckband Earphones: The Reliable Workhorse</h2><p><strong>Battery life is king.</strong> Most neckbands deliver 20-40 hours of playback on a single charge. Some like the boAt Rockerz series push beyond 50 hours. You can charge them on Sunday and not worry until next weekend.</p><p><strong>They stay put.</strong> The band sits around your neck, so there is zero chance of dropping an earbud while running, commuting, or working out. When you are not listening, they just hang around your neck — no case needed.</p><p><strong>Better call quality.</strong> The mic sits closer to your mouth compared to TWS earbuds, which means clearer voice pickup during calls.</p><h2>TWS Earbuds: The Compact Powerhouse</h2><p><strong>True freedom.</strong> No wires, no band, nothing touching your neck. They sit in your ears and disappear. Perfect for workouts, office use, and casual listening.</p><p><strong>Features galore.</strong> ANC, transparency mode, in-ear detection, touch controls, wireless charging cases — TWS earbuds pack serious tech into tiny packages.</p><p><strong>Style factor.</strong> Let us be honest — TWS earbuds look sleeker. The compact charging case fits in any pocket.</p><h2>Head-to-Head Comparison</h2><p><strong>Battery:</strong> Neckband wins (20-50 hrs vs 5-8 hrs per charge)<br><strong>Portability:</strong> TWS wins (pocket-sized case vs bulky band)<br><strong>Sound Quality:</strong> Tie (both excellent at similar price points)<br><strong>Call Quality:</strong> Neckband wins (mic closer to mouth)<br><strong>Features:</strong> TWS wins (ANC, touch controls, wear detection)<br><strong>Workout Use:</strong> Depends (neckband for running, TWS for gym)<br><strong>Price:</strong> Neckband wins (more features per rupee)</p><h2>So Which Should You Buy?</h2><p><strong>Buy a neckband if:</strong> You need long battery life, make a lot of calls, commute by metro or bus, or want a reliable daily driver that you never have to worry about charging.</p><p><strong>Buy TWS earbuds if:</strong> You want the latest features like ANC, prefer a compact form factor, use them for short listening sessions, or want something stylish for office and gym use.</p><p><strong>The sweet spot?</strong> Own both. A neckband for daily commutes and calls, and TWS earbuds for workouts and weekends. At Jikra, you can grab a quality neckband and TWS pair together for under ₹3000.</p><blockquote>There is no wrong choice — only the right choice for your daily routine. Check out our neckband and TWS collections at Jikra to compare options side by side.</blockquote>',
