            [
                'title'          => 'Best Power Banks in India 2026: 10000mAh vs 20000mAh — Complete Buying Guide',
                'slug'           => 'best-power-banks-india-buying-guide',
                'category'       => 'Power Banks',
                'tags'           => ['power bank', 'best power bank india', '10000mAh power bank', '20000mAh power bank', 'fast charging power bank', 'portable charger'],
                'featured_image' => 'blog/blog-power-banks.jpg',
                'excerpt'        => 'Which power bank capacity is right for you? We compare 10000mAh vs 20000mAh power banks, explain fast charging support, and recommend the best options from Anker, Mi, Ambrane, and boAt.',
                'content'        => '<h2>Do You Really Need a Power Bank in 2026?</h2><p>Despite bigger phone batteries, our screen time has also increased. Between social media, navigation, UPI payments, and streaming, most of us drain our phones before dinner. A power bank is not a luxury — it is insurance against dead phones, missed cab bookings, and failed UPI payments at the worst possible moments.</p><h2>Understanding mAh: What the Numbers Actually Mean</h2><p>mAh (milliamp hours) measures how much charge a power bank holds. But here is what most people miss: a 10000mAh power bank does not give you 10000mAh of usable charge. Energy is lost during voltage conversion and heat. In practice:</p><ul><li><strong>10000mAh</strong> = About 2-2.5 full charges for a 4500mAh phone</li><li><strong>20000mAh</strong> = About 4.5-5 full charges</li><li><strong>5000mAh</strong> = About 1-1.2 full charges (emergency backup only)</li></ul><h2>10000mAh vs 20000mAh: Which to Choose?</h2><h3>10000mAh Power Banks</h3><p><strong>Best for:</strong> Daily commuters, college students, casual users<br><strong>Weight:</strong> 200-250g (pocket-friendly)<br><strong>Size:</strong> About the size of a smartphone<br><strong>Charges:</strong> 2-2.5 full phone charges<br><strong>Price range:</strong> ₹699-₹1499</p><p>This is the sweet spot for most people. Light enough to carry daily, powerful enough for a full day away from the plug. Slip it in your bag and forget about battery anxiety.</p><h3>20000mAh Power Banks</h3><p><strong>Best for:</strong> Travellers, power users, content creators, multi-device users<br><strong>Weight:</strong> 400-500g<br><strong>Size:</strong> Noticeably larger — fits in a bag, not a pocket<br><strong>Charges:</strong> 4.5-5 full phone charges<br><strong>Price range:</strong> ₹1299-₹2499</p><p>If you travel frequently, charge multiple devices, or simply hate running out of juice, 20000mAh is your friend. Just be aware — they are heavier and take longer to recharge (6-8 hours at 18W input).</p><h2>Key Features to Look For</h2><p><strong>Fast charging output:</strong> 18W QC or 20W PD means your phone charges at full speed, not slow trickle mode.<br><strong>Fast charging input:</strong> This determines how quickly the power bank itself recharges. 18W+ input is ideal.<br><strong>USB-C port:</strong> Universal, reversible, and increasingly the only cable you need.<br><strong>Multiple outputs:</strong> Charge two or three devices simultaneously.<br><strong>LED indicator:</strong> Shows remaining charge level at a glance.</p><h2>Top Power Bank Brands in India</h2><p><strong>Anker:</strong> Premium quality, excellent safety features. Best for iPhone and Samsung users who want reliable PD charging.<br><strong>Mi/Redmi:</strong> Great value. Their 10000mAh and 20000mAh options are bestsellers for a reason.<br><strong>Ambrane:</strong> India\'s most popular power bank brand. Wide range from budget to premium.<br><strong>boAt:</strong> Stylish designs with fast charging. Great for younger buyers who want looks and performance.</p><blockquote>A power bank is only useful if you actually carry it. Pick the capacity that matches your lifestyle, not the biggest number. Shop power banks with fast charging at Jikra — free shipping above ₹499.</blockquote>',
