            [
                'title'          => 'Tempered Glass vs Screen Protector: What Actually Protects Your Phone Screen?',
                'slug'           => 'tempered-glass-vs-screen-protector-guide',
                'category'       => 'Screen Protectors',
                'tags'           => ['tempered glass', 'screen protector', 'screen guard', 'phone screen protection', 'matte screen guard', 'privacy screen'],
                'featured_image' => 'blog/blog-screen-protectors.jpg',
                'excerpt'        => 'Is tempered glass really better than a plastic screen protector? What about matte and privacy options? This guide covers every type of screen protection so you can make the right choice.',
                'content'        => '<h2>Screen Repairs Are Expensive — Prevention Is Cheap</h2><p>A cracked phone screen repair costs ₹3000-₹15000 depending on your phone model. An AMOLED screen replacement on a flagship phone can exceed ₹20000. Meanwhile, a quality tempered glass costs ₹199-₹499. The math is simple — screen protection is the smartest investment you can make for your phone.</p><h2>Types of Screen Protection</h2><h3>Tempered Glass</h3><p><strong>Protection level:</strong> Highest<br><strong>Hardness:</strong> 9H (just below diamond at 10H)<br><strong>Feel:</strong> Smooth, feels like the actual screen<br><strong>Price:</strong> ₹149-₹599</p><p>Tempered glass is regular glass that has been heat-treated for extra strength. When it takes an impact, the tempered glass cracks instead of your actual screen — sacrificing itself to save your phone. This is the gold standard in screen protection and what we recommend for everyone.</p><h3>PET Film / Plastic Screen Guard</h3><p><strong>Protection level:</strong> Low (scratches only, no drop protection)<br><strong>Hardness:</strong> 2H-3H<br><strong>Feel:</strong> Slightly rubbery, attracts fingerprints<br><strong>Price:</strong> ₹49-₹149</p><p>These thin plastic films prevent scratches but offer zero drop protection. They are cheap but you get what you pay for. Only worth considering as a temporary solution until you get proper tempered glass.</p><h3>Matte / Anti-Glare Tempered Glass</h3><p><strong>Best for:</strong> Outdoor use, gamers, people who hate fingerprints<br><strong>Trade-off:</strong> Slightly reduces screen clarity and colour vibrancy</p><p>Matte tempered glass has a frosted finish that eliminates glare and reduces fingerprint smudges. Gamers love it because thumbs glide smoothly without sticking. Outdoor workers appreciate the reduced glare in sunlight. The downside is a slight haze effect on the screen.</p><h3>Privacy Tempered Glass</h3><p><strong>Best for:</strong> Banking, confidential work, metro commuters<br><strong>How it works:</strong> Darkens the screen at side angles (beyond 30 degrees)</p><p>Tired of strangers reading your WhatsApp in the metro? Privacy screen protectors use micro-louver technology to make your screen visible only when looking straight at it. Side viewers see a dark screen. Essential for banking professionals, lawyers, and anyone handling sensitive information on their phone.</p><h3>Camera Lens Protectors</h3><p><strong>Often overlooked but equally important.</strong> Phone camera bumps are raised and exposed — the first thing to scratch when you place your phone on a surface. A ₹99-₹199 camera lens protector prevents scratches that permanently affect your photo quality.</p><h2>How to Apply Tempered Glass Perfectly</h2><ol><li>Clean your screen with the wet wipe, then the dry wipe</li><li>Use the dust absorber sticker to remove any remaining particles</li><li>Align the tempered glass with your phone\'s camera and speaker cutouts</li><li>Let it fall naturally — the adhesive side clings to the screen automatically</li><li>Press from the centre outward to push out any air bubbles</li></ol><p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Apply in a steam-filled bathroom (run hot water for 2 minutes). The steam settles dust particles in the air, preventing them from getting trapped under the glass.</p><blockquote>Think of tempered glass as a ₹299 insurance policy for your ₹15000+ phone screen. Replace it whenever it cracks — that crack means it did its job. Shop screen protectors for your phone model at Jikra.</blockquote>',
                'is_published'   => true,
                'published_at'   => now()->subDays(14),
                'view_count'     => 823,
                'seo_data'       => [
                    'meta_title'       => 'Tempered Glass vs Screen Protector: Complete Guide | Jikra Blog',
                    'meta_description' => 'Tempered glass or plastic screen guard? Compare protection levels, types (matte, privacy, camera lens), and learn the perfect application technique. Screen protection guide.',
                ],
            ],

