            [
                'title'          => 'Smartwatch vs Fitness Band: Which Wearable Is Right for You?',
                'slug'           => 'smartwatch-vs-fitness-band-comparison',
                'category'       => 'Smartwatches & Bands',
                'tags'           => ['fitness band', 'smartwatch vs band', 'Mi Band', 'fitness tracker', 'wearable comparison', 'health tracking'],
                'featured_image' => 'blog/blog-smartwatch-vs-band.jpg',
                'excerpt'        => 'Smartwatch or fitness band? Both track your health, but they serve different purposes. This comparison helps you decide based on your priorities — fitness tracking, notifications, budget, and style.',
                'content'        => '<h2>Two Wearables, Two Philosophies</h2><p>Smartwatches and fitness bands both live on your wrist and track your health. But they approach the job differently. A fitness band is a focused health tracker that happens to show notifications. A smartwatch is a mini phone on your wrist that happens to track health. The right choice depends on what you value most.</p><h2>Fitness Bands: The Essentialist Choice</h2><p><strong>Strengths:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Battery life:</strong> 10-20 days is standard. Some stretch to 30 days. Charge it twice a month and forget about it.</li><li><strong>Lightweight:</strong> 15-25 grams. You forget it is there, which means you actually wear it 24/7 including during sleep.</li><li><strong>Affordable:</strong> ₹1499-₹3499 for top-tier bands. The Xiaomi Smart Band series starts under ₹2000.</li><li><strong>Sleep tracking:</strong> Because they are so lightweight, they are more comfortable for overnight wear.</li><li><strong>Durability:</strong> Smaller, lighter, and less exposed to damage.</li></ul><p><strong>Limitations:</strong> Small screen (hard to read long messages), no Bluetooth calling, limited app support, fewer watch face options.</p><h2>Smartwatches: The Feature-Rich Choice</h2><p><strong>Strengths:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Large display:</strong> 1.3-1.96 inch screens make notifications, maps, and messages easy to read.</li><li><strong>Bluetooth calling:</strong> Answer and make calls from your wrist. Game-changer when your phone is in your bag.</li><li><strong>App ecosystem:</strong> Calculator, weather, music control, camera remote, and more.</li><li><strong>Style:</strong> Looks like a real watch. Swappable straps for different occasions.</li><li><strong>More sensors:</strong> Some offer GPS, compass, and temperature sensors.</li></ul><p><strong>Limitations:</strong> Shorter battery life (3-7 days typical), heavier (40-60g), higher price point, more fragile screen.</p><h2>Feature Comparison Table</h2><p><strong>Battery Life:</strong> Band (14-20 days) vs Watch (3-7 days)<br><strong>Display Size:</strong> Band (1.0-1.1 inch) vs Watch (1.3-1.96 inch)<br><strong>Weight:</strong> Band (15-25g) vs Watch (40-60g)<br><strong>Bluetooth Calling:</strong> Band (No) vs Watch (Yes)<br><strong>Price Range:</strong> Band (₹1499-₹3499) vs Watch (₹1999-₹4999)<br><strong>Heart Rate:</strong> Both (Yes)<br><strong>SpO2:</strong> Both (Yes)<br><strong>Sleep Tracking:</strong> Band (Better comfort) vs Watch (More detailed data)<br><strong>Style Factor:</strong> Band (Sporty) vs Watch (Versatile)</p><h2>Decision Guide</h2><p><strong>Choose a fitness band if:</strong></p><ul><li>Fitness and health tracking is your primary goal</li><li>You want to wear it 24/7 including during sleep without discomfort</li><li>Long battery life matters more than features</li><li>You are budget-conscious</li><li>You already have a regular watch you love wearing</li></ul><p><strong>Choose a smartwatch if:</strong></p><ul><li>You want Bluetooth calling on your wrist</li><li>You need to read and reply to notifications easily</li><li>Style and versatility matter — one device for gym and office</li><li>You want a larger, more readable display</li><li>You do not mind charging every few days</li></ul><h2>Our Recommendation</h2><p>For most people in 2026, a budget smartwatch under ₹3000-₹5000 gives you the best of both worlds — decent health tracking AND smart features. But if you are a serious fitness enthusiast who wants maximum comfort and battery life, a premium fitness band is hard to beat.</p><blockquote>The best wearable is the one you actually wear every day. Browse smartwatches and fitness bands at Jikra to find your perfect match.</blockquote>',
                'is_published'   => true,
                'published_at'   => now()->subDays(10),
                'view_count'     => 589,
                'seo_data'       => [
                    'meta_title'       => 'Smartwatch vs Fitness Band: Which Should You Buy? | Jikra Blog',
                    'meta_description' => 'Smartwatch or fitness band? Compare battery life, features, comfort, price & health tracking. Complete guide to help you choose the right wearable for your lifestyle.',
